    part budgetVerdictTellsExhaustedFromNoneImplementGateR1 : TestResult { :>> id = "50502860-9c87-4e0f-b950-78366bda792b"; :>> outcome = VerdictKind::pass; :>> judgedAgainst = "c8df10d"; :>> judgedAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> judgedBy = "claudeFable5"; }
    verification budgetVerdictTellsExhaustedFromNoneReviewGate : Test { :>> id = "874e29c8-bc8a-4df8-8b2b-4a23b6e1f7b2"; :>> title = "Sprint 695 review gate — three passes per D0172"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Three passes (D0172). Correctness: the verdict is decided by two facts the run records (the prefix, turns used against the budget) and never by the tools list, so a `budget` cannot be produced by a turn that made no Skill call - the third probe case holds that edge; a route or a wrong call at the last turn still wins over `budget` because score returns before the budget test - the fourth and fifth cases hold those. The five cases were chosen before the run and the run was paid for only after they held. Honesty: the finding is ROUTED 3/3 at 6 turns and is recorded as an investigation's finding on the item that motivated it, not as a rate and not as a TestResult of the release skill; the 3-turn `none` of 2026-09-09 and 2026-09-10 is not rewritten - the receipts of sprints 638 and 656 stand, and this receipt says what they were reading. Scope: routing_probe.py only; the DoD on dcPrefixLeavesRoomForTheRoute (created by claudeOpus5) is not edited (D0108/D0307) - the disallowed-Bash cause issue456 asked the DoD to name is carried in the receipt instead. Residual: the `budget` verdict reads the turn count, not why the turns were spent; a prefix that spends six turns searching would score `budget` again, and that would be the next Issue against the check, not a route finding."; }
