    verification budgetVerdictTellsExhaustedFromNoneRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "420f53ad-6b9a-4e74-a548-f42c5ef6b0ed"; :>> title = "Sprint 695 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "AVOIDABLE-ISSUE SCAN (D0131): the samples show one empirical thing beyond the DoD - every sample spent one or two ToolSearch turns hunting for the instrument the intake prefix's procedure names, because the rig disallows Bash (issue456's cause). At 6 turns the route survives that; at 3 it did not. That cost is the sandbox's, not the skill's, and it is paid on every run of every case whose prefix is intake. Tracked as issue519 (Medium): the rig's sandbox removes the instrument the declared prefix's procedure runs, so every intake-prefixed sample spends turns on a search the real agent never makes; resolver dcRigSandboxKeepsThePrefixInstrument - a stub or allowed read-only `keel record statement --dry-run` path so the prefix completes in one turn, probed before and after with the same release case. Not a Decision: it is a one-off defect of the check with a measured basis, an Issue first."; }
